00:32:31.390 --> 00:32:32.560
It goes in both directions

00:32:32.560 --> 00:32:34.640
when you're in a group or a class,

00:32:34.640 --> 00:32:35.473
you're sharing

00:32:35.473 --> 00:32:36.957
and you're being shared with,

00:32:36.957 --> 00:32:40.780
and the power of that is really

00:32:40.780 --> 00:32:43.150
exponentially, I think increased

00:32:43.150 --> 00:32:45.870
when you relate to the people around you,

00:32:45.870 --> 00:32:47.160
when you feel seen

00:32:47.160 --> 00:32:50.774
and you feel that that shared experience.

00:32:50.774 --> 00:32:52.120
- Yeah, yeah, that's huge.

00:32:52.120 --> 00:32:53.460
And I think it goes a long way in building

00:32:53.460 --> 00:32:55.140
that level of trust too,

00:32:55.140 --> 00:32:55.973
that's really important

00:32:55.973 --> 00:32:58.130
and moving forward in a lot of ways.

00:32:58.130 --> 00:32:58.963
Through the challenges,

00:32:58.963 --> 00:32:59.796
'cause they are challenging.

00:32:59.796 --> 00:33:00.950
If the trust isn't there,

00:33:00.950 --> 00:33:02.070
I think it makes it that much harder

00:33:02.070 --> 00:33:04.210
for people to really engage

00:33:04.210 --> 00:33:05.300
and Corey it sounds like you all

00:33:05.300 --> 00:33:07.020
had that in the group too.

00:33:07.020 --> 00:33:09.370
Just the relate-ability there,

00:33:09.370 --> 00:33:10.630
it seems like there
was some level of trust

00:33:10.630 --> 00:33:11.540
that came with that as well,

00:33:11.540 --> 00:33:12.720
because, oh, these are other people

00:33:12.720 --> 00:33:14.660
who can relate to what I've been through

00:33:14.660 --> 00:33:15.650
and we can trust each other

00:33:15.650 --> 00:33:16.810
to learn from each other

00:33:16.810 --> 00:33:17.750
